{
  "description": "The secrets endpoints model `secrets` as an object whose only properties are the example secret names (STRIPE, ALGOLIA, DATABASE, USER), so the update request rejects any other name at the type level and the list and update responses expose no other name. On the wire `secrets` is a dictionary keyed by secret name: the Doppler CLI sends `{\"secrets\": {\"NAME\": null}}` to delete a secret (DopplerHQ/cli pkg/cmd/secrets.go:438-443) and parses both the list and the update response as map<name, secret> (pkg/models/api.go:156-170). Each secret in those maps is the object GET /v3/configs/config/secret returns (https://docs.doppler.com/reference/secrets-list): rawVisibility is the string enum unmasked/masked/restricted and computedVisibility a string, not the `{type}` objects the list schema declares (its own example is the string \"masked\"), and it carries rawValueType and computedValueType (live GET /v3/configs/config/secrets, 2026-10-13). `raw` and `computed` are null for restricted secrets read with a user token (https://docs.doppler.com/docs/secret-visibility; DopplerHQ/terraform-provider-doppler doppler/resource_secret.go:136-149) and are secret values. In `change_requests`, `originalName` and `value` take `null` as the spec's own descriptions say, `originalName` may be omitted for new secrets, and `value` and `originalValue` are secret values.",
